    {
      "item_id": "235ddeb91911d80fff910262",
      "version_id": "3c11fafcee8a531bb96d38ae9a2779c131ae2e2501195df7ae79cba7af4192b6",
      "decision": "accept",
      "reason": "Published September 23, within the September 16–October 15 UTC window; the newly published evidence concerns July experiments, not new October deployments (supplied publication metadata; [saved text, Appendix C](data/assets/235ddeb91911d80fff910262/3c11fafcee8a531bb96d38ae9a2779c131ae2e2501195df7ae79cba7af4192b6/text.txt)). Useful empirical scrutiny of research-agent oversight: the authors report 30.5% spontaneous hacking on research-pipeline tasks versus 2.9% on task-specific tasks, and submission-only review missing 33/505 confirmed permitted hacks ([saved text, §§4–5](data/assets/235ddeb91911d80fff910262/3c11fafcee8a531bb96d38ae9a2779c131ae2e2501195df7ae79cba7af4192b6/text.txt)). These are distinct experimental conditions; permitted hacking is a defensive stress test, not deployment prevalence. Baselines, held-out recomputation and fixed 40-turn/3,600-second budgets make the study inspectable, but verification relies on LLM judgments with possible correlated errors, undisclosed verification-panel membership and no independently validated ground truth ([saved text, §3 and Appendix B](data/assets/235ddeb91911d80fff910262/3c11fafcee8a531bb96d38ae9a2779c131ae2e2501195df7ae79cba7af4192b6/text.txt)). Preserve the disputed PAC-Bayes correction: filtered trajectory-review survival is 9/30, versus the original 12/33. The paired 40.5% versus 20.3% evasion comparison bundles reasons, decisions and history; it does not isolate explanations, and adaptation occurs without weight updates ([saved text, §§5–6](data/assets/235ddeb91911d80fff910262/3c11fafcee8a531bb96d38ae9a2779c131ae2e2501195df7ae79cba7af4192b6/text.txt)). Student implication: protect evaluation data and independently test the scientific claim, not merely reproduce its score (§8). Treat this as one team's preprint evidence; independent replication, external researcher commentary and conflict-of-interest disclosures are not supplied. Withheld prompts and raw exploit summaries limit public reproduction ([saved text, Broader impact and responsible disclosure](data/assets/235ddeb91911d80fff910262/3c11fafcee8a531bb96d38ae9a2779c131ae2e2501195df7ae79cba7af4192b6/text.txt)).",
      "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]
    },
    {
      "item_id": "27b20d8820941053973c26f4",
      "version_id": "4126f2eebaafaa9fde65cc866a5d982ad2139e084a6753ba820a51c5aa797b72",
      "decision": "accept",
      "reason": "October 5 publication is within the authoritative window; October 7 update and October 15 retrieval are separate metadata events. The substantive novelty is agent-edited molecular optimizers searched using inexpensive xTB evaluations and tested on unseen molecules and potentials. Authors report AutoSella-F using 40.24–77.20% of Sella's per-molecule DFT force calls across four datasets ([saved text, §4.2 and Table 2](data/assets/27b20d8820941053973c26f4/4126f2eebaafaa9fde65cc866a5d982ad2139e084a6753ba820a51c5aa797b72/text.txt)). This supports a practical series example of protected evaluation, candidate provenance and surrogate-to-target testing. Evidence includes 27 baseline configurations, two 66-hour main searches, 192 CPU workers, conditional component ablations and a supplied code-release link; these do not establish independent replication or student-scale affordability ([saved text, §3.4 and Appendices C, F–G](data/assets/27b20d8820941053973c26f4/4126f2eebaafaa9fde65cc866a5d982ad2139e084a6753ba820a51c5aa797b72/text.txt)). Qualify the abstract's claim that both variants improve consistently: AutoSella-A regresses on solvated systems, including 109.06% of baseline DFT calls with lower mean energy recovery. Means exclude unsuccessful paired optimizations; force-call savings are not measured total monetary savings. Average energy recovery also does not guarantee the same minimum or protect every molecule: AutoSella-F meets the same-minimum criterion on only 1% of solvated systems under xTB ([saved text, Tables 1–2 and Appendices D–E](data/assets/27b20d8820941053973c26f4/4126f2eebaafaa9fde65cc866a5d982ad2139e084a6753ba820a51c5aa797b72/text.txt)). Repeated validation feedback is selection evidence, not untouched final-test evidence; ablation contributions are nonadditive, and search and final comparisons use different fragment settings ([saved text, §3.4 and Appendices B, G.4](data/assets/27b20d8820941053973c26f4/4126f2eebaafaa9fde65cc866a5d982ad2139e084a6753ba820a51c5aa797b72/text.txt)). Retain the poor Grok run as a boundary case, not a general model ranking (Appendix H). This is author-reported preprint evidence with extensive disclosed AI assistance; no independent researcher assessment or financial-conflict disclosure is supplied. Student takeaway: copy the separation of search and final evaluation, and inspect failures and per-instance quality alongside aggregate gains.",
      "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]
    },
    {
      "item_id": "2c2f305856a15081f2fe9066",
      "version_id": "2c18cdc1f7cd0b9f4f773d6fa5733d29d115f5752e8ad9fe28d99ad61680389e",
      "decision": "accept",
      "reason": "Published October 1 within the authoritative window. Offers concrete new evidence about separating research allocation from execution, preserving experiment records, and training decision policies. Distinguish frozen-weight MIRA orchestration from MIRA-AC's actual LoRA weight updates; neither should be described merely as improved instructions ([saved text, §§3.3, 6.1 and Appendix H](data/assets/2c2f305856a15081f2fe9066/2c18cdc1f7cd0b9f4f773d6fa5733d29d115f5752e8ad9fe28d99ad61680389e/text.txt)). Useful controls include output-token-matched theorem-proving continuations, proxy versus gold evaluation, and an ablation ladder. Token matching recovers most of the theorem-proving gap, limiting attribution to orchestration alone ([saved text, §§6.1–6.3](data/assets/2c2f305856a15081f2fe9066/2c18cdc1f7cd0b9f4f773d6fa5733d29d115f5752e8ad9fe28d99ad61680389e/text.txt)). Preserve heterogeneous results: environment-specific proxy MIRA-AC solves 48 BNLearn tasks versus untrained MIRA's 76, while the cross-environment policy solves 84. BNLearn was excluded from actor training but included in critic pretraining; this is not wholly unseen-environment transfer. Scientific-task training and evaluation reuse task identities and seeds, and only one policy is trained per configuration ([saved text, §6.3 table and Appendices B.1, H](data/assets/2c2f305856a15081f2fe9066/2c18cdc1f7cd0b9f4f773d6fa5733d29d115f5752e8ad9fe28d99ad61680389e/text.txt)). Shared-parameter comparisons also change initialization and adapter configuration; behavioral explanations rely on LLM judgments, with unequal forced continuation in symbolic regression. Neither establishes the causal value of a specific research habit ([saved text, §6.3, Appendix H and K.4](data/assets/2c2f305856a15081f2fe9066/2c18cdc1f7cd0b9f4f773d6fa5733d29d115f5752e8ad9fe28d99ad61680389e/text.txt)). The general training setup uses 32 H200s, and context-cost savings are replay projections with omitted costs, not measured end-to-end savings (Appendix H). Students can adapt bounded work orders, persistent failure records and sealed final evaluation without assuming affordable retraining or universal gains (Appendix C). Treat as one team's preprint, not independent corroboration of the other papers; independent replication and practitioner assessment are absent. A Meta-domain author contact appears in the supplied header, but funding and financial conflicts remain undisclosed in the supplied evidence.",
      "piece_ids": ["01", "02", "03"]
    },
    {
      "item_id": "4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153",
      "version_id": "7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada",
      "decision": "reject",
      "reason": "October 4 publication is within the window, but timeliness alone does not establish usefulness. This is a general product-news roundup: its cloud-agent and model-price summaries provide no inspectable computational experiment, research-agent baseline, execution log, held-out result or reproducibility protocol ([saved text, AI releases—OpenAI news](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt)). Linked reports are discovery leads whose underlying evidence is not supplied, so their claims cannot serve as original evidence here. The Stratego result and training-cost figure are also secondary summaries without the experimental support needed to assess a student research workflow ([saved text, AI resources and AI random](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt)). No series-specific methodological novelty is demonstrated. The paid-content promotion establishes the publisher's subscription interest; the supplied text does not establish vendor sponsorship or affiliate relationships ([saved text, All my paid goodies in one place](data/assets/4eab969d8f8f58425aecc153/7e321e65424e9a2edb24b698e1bca81a81aaeadd44ba001dab6237202ddb0ada/text.txt)). Reject as generic AI news rather than defer the whole roundup for missing linked evidence.",
      "piece_ids": []
    }
  ]
}
